error[NK1301]: `.to_string()` on a text literal adds nothing.
  --> tests/literal_to_string_refused.nika:3:5
   |
 3 |     let a = "-p".to_string()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A text literal is already the text wherever text is wanted.
   = help: Drop `.to_string()`.
error[NK1301]: `.clone()` on a text literal adds nothing.
  --> tests/literal_to_string_refused.nika:4:5
   |
 4 |     let b = "-q".clone()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A text literal is already the text wherever text is wanted.
   = help: Drop `.clone()`.
error[NK1301]: `.to_string()` on text adds nothing.
  --> tests/literal_to_string_refused.nika:7:13
   |
 7 |     let t = a.to_string()
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A view is a `String` already, and the compiler decides whether text is a view or text of its own (Part I 2.3).
   = help: Drop `.to_string()`, or write `.clone()` where a copy is meant; `nikaia fix` drops it.
3 type errors
